            = succeed "-theoretic/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            spirit. The expected alternative definition in terms of action morphisms has been considered (and is well known) apparently only for special cases.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#representations Representations
          %p
            Recall that we take, by definition,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-algebroids"} Lie ∞-algebroids
            to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dual
            to non-negatively-graded, graded-commutative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded+algebra"} differential algebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CE
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE_A(g)
            for the qDGCA whose underlying graded-commutative algebra is the free (over the algebra
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet g^*
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            a non-postively graded cochain complex of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^*
            its degree-wise dual over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-algebroid"} Lie ∞-algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            whose space of objects is characterized dually by the algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong representation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              of a Lie
              = succeed "-algebroid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g, A)
              on a co-chain complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              of
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+sequence"} fibration sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi CE
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi CE
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\wedge^\bullet V \leftarrow CE_\rho(g,V) \leftarrow CE_A(g)
            %p in DGCAs, i.e. a homotopy pushout
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ∧
                              %mo •
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi CE
                              %mi ρ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi CE
                              %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\wedge^\bullet V &amp;\leftarrow&amp; CE_\rho(g)
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                    \\\
                    0 &amp;\leftarrow &amp; CE_A(g)
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            What has been considered in the literature so far is the more restrictive version, where the pushout is taken to be strict (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs
            \: at least I think that this is the right way to say it):
          %p
            A
            %strong proper representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            is a strict cofiber sequence of morphisms of DGCAs
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mi V
                  %mo ←
                  %msub
                    %mi CE
                    %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ←
                  %msub
                    %mi CE
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\wedge^\bullet V \leftarrow CE_\rho(g,V) \leftarrow CE_A(g)
          %p i.e. such that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi CE
                        %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi CE
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo •
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE_\rho(g,V) = CE_A(g) \otimes \wedge^\bullet V
                as GCAs
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo •
                      %mi V
                      %mo ←
                      %msub
                        %mi CE
                        %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet V \leftarrow CE_\rho(g,V)
                is the obvious surjection;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi CE
                        %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ←
                      %msub
                        %mi CE
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE_\rho(g,V) \leftarrow CE_A(g)
                is the obvious injection;
            %li
              %p the composite of both is the 0-map.
          %p
            It follows that the differential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_\rho
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CE
                    %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE_\rho(g,V)
            is given by a
            %strong twisting map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho^* : V \to (\wedge^\bullet V) \wedge (g^*) \wedge (\wedge^\bullet g^*)
            as
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi ρ
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi g
                            %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_\rho|_{g^*} = d_g
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi ρ
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi V
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi V
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_\rho|_{V} = d_V + \rho^*
          %p which may be thought of as the dual of the representation morphism (see the examples below).
          %h3#dgcategory_of_representations dg-Category of representations
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#Block05"}> Block 05
            ) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rep
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(g,A)
            of proper representations of a Lie-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g,A)
            in the above sense – called
            %em dg-algebra modules
            there – is defined.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Given two objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CE
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE_\rho(g,V)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CE
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE_{\rho'}(g,V')
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Rep
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(g,A)
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi CE
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi CE
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom( CE_\rho(g,V),  CE_{\rho'}(g,V') )
            %p
              consist in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              of morphisms of degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi g
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi : V \otimes \wedge^\bullet g \to V' \otimes \wedge^\bullet g^*
            %p
              satisfying
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(v t) = (-1)^{k |a|} \phi(v) t
            %p
              and the differential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi Hom
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{Hom}
              is the usual differential on hom-complexes
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mrow
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo ′
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi ρ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \phi = d_{\rho'} \circ \phi - (-1)^{|\phi|} \phi \circ d_\rho
            %p
              For a fixed Lie
              = succeed "-algebroid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g,A)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Rep
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Rep(g,A)
            %p
              with Lie representations of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g,A)
              as objects and chain comoplexes as above as hom-objects is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#basic Basic
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For an n ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+representation"} Lie algebra representation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              on a vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CE
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE_\rho(g,V)
              that computes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          #ActionOfTangentLieAlgebroid.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connections"} flat connections
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
              exhibits a representation of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroid"} tangent Lie algebroid
              of the base manifold.
          %p
            A holomorphic variant of this is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ActionOfHolomorphicTangentAlgebroid"} below
          %ul
            %li
              (…)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+representation"} adjoint representation
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E-algebras"} algebras
          %h3#ActionOfHolomorphicTangentAlgebroid Action of holomorphic tangent Lie algebroid on chain complexes of complex vector bundles
          %p
            The following variant of example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ActionOfTangentLieAlgebroid"}
            is a
            = succeed "-refinement" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy-theoretic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Koszul-Malgrange+theorem"} Koszul-Malgrange theorem
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi hol
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g,A) = T_{hol} X
              the holomorphic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroid"} tangent Lie algebroid
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CE
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi hol
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE_A(g) = \Omega^\bullet_{hol}(X) = \Omega^{\bullet,0}(X)
              the holomorphic part of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dolbeault+complex"} Dolbeault complex
              of
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Rep
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi hol
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(T_{hol} X)
              taken to have as objects complexes of
              %em finitely generated
              and
              %em projective
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mi Rep
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi hol
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho Rep(T_{hol} X)
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Rep
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi hol
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(T_{hol} X)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to the
              %em
                bounded
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaves"} abelian sheaves
                with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+cohomology"} coherent cohomology
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (see at
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaf"} coherent sheaf
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Block05"} Block 05, theorem 2.22
            (in the counting of version 1 on the arXiv!)).
          %p
            The objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rep
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi hol
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(T_{hol} X)
            are literally complexes of smooth vector bundles that are equipped with “half a flat connection”, namely with a flat covariant derivative only along holomorphic tangent vectors. It is an old result that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+vector+bundles"} holomorphic vector bundles
            (see there) are equivalent to such smooth vector bundles with “half a flat connection”. This is what the theorem is based on.
          %h3#Extensions
            Extensions of
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
              any other,then an
              %a{:href => "infinity-Lie+algebra+cohomology#Extensions"} L-∞ extension
              (see there)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat {\mathfrak{g}}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequence"} homotopy fiber sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathfrak{a} \to \hat {\mathfrak{g}} \to \mathfrak{g}
            %p
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
              (see at
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} model structure for L-∞ algebras
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebroids"} L-∞ algebroids
              over the point
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi 𝔞
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{B}\mathfrak{a} \to \mathbf{B}\hat {\mathfrak{g}} \to \mathbf{B}\mathfrak{g}
            %p
              and then passing to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              on the
              = succeed "-algebroid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi 𝔞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathfrak{a}
          %p
            For instance the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+Lie+2-algebra"} string Lie 2-algebra
            is the
            = succeed "-extension" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} \mathbb{R}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            with bilinear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -,-\rangle
            corresponding to the 3-cocycle
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -,[-,-]\rangle \in CE(\mathfrak{g})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbb{R}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
            of a simply connected compact simple
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-group"} circle 2-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1)
            which exhibits the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+2-group"} String 2-group
            extension.
          %p
            Analogous statements in various degrees hold for the
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fivebrane+6-group"} Fivebrane 6-group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 6
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔣𝔦𝔳𝔢𝔟𝔯𝔞𝔫𝔢
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔰𝔱𝔯𝔦𝔫𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}^6 \mathbb{R} \to \mathfrak{fivebrane}\to \mathfrak{string}
          %p
            exhibiting an
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+Lie+2-algebra"} string Lie 2-algebra
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 7
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^7 \mathbb{R}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+6-algebra"} supergravity Lie 6-algebra
            and for all the other extensions in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} The brane bouquet
          %h2#relations_to_comodules_over_the_ce_coalgebra Relations to (co-)modules over the CE (co-)algebra
          %p
            Under identifying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebras"} L-infinity algebras
            with graded (co-)commutative
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-coalgebras"} dg-coalgebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebras"} dg-algebras
            (their
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-comodules"} model structure on dg-comodules
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-modules"} model structure on dg-modules
          %h2#References References
          %p
            The definition of representation of
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Lada"}> Tom Lada
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Markl"} Martin Markl
              %em Strongly homotopy Lie algebras
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9406095"}> arXiv:9406095
              )
          %p
            The general definition of representation of
            = succeed "-Lie" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              %em Differential twisted string- and fivebrane structures
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0910.4001v1"}> arXiv:0910.4001 version 1
              )
          %p
            (this discussion is not in the published version
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0910.4001v2"} arXiv:0910.4001v2
          %p following
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              \:
              %em
                On
                = succeed "-Lie" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              (2008) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/schreiber/action.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Schreiber-InfinityLie.pdf", :title => ""} Schreiber-InfinityLie.pdf
          %p
            and modeled after the general abstract definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-actions"} ∞-actions
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"} Danny Stevenson
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles+--+theory%2C+presentations+and+applications"} Principal ∞-bundles – theory, presentations and applications
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1207.0248"} arXiv:1207.0248
          %p The definition of the dg-category of representation of a tangent Lie algebroid and its equivalence in special cases to derived categories of complexes of coherent sheaves is in
          %ul
            %li#Block05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Block"}> Jonathan Block
              ,
              %em Duality and equivalence of module categories in noncommutative geometry I
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0509284"}> arXiv:0509284
              )
          %p
            Application of this to the description of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-branes"} B-branes
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Bergman08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Bergman"}> Aaron Bergman
              ,
              %em Topological D-branes from Descent
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0808.0168"}> arXiv:0808.0168
              )
